From aec094beaaf4683ad5ecf3e4e210c6a8565e21f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: razgulay <bantran09@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:22:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fix(transport,translator): enforce the Gemini role
 contract + probe silent HTTP/2 connections
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two upstream-failure classes on heavy Gemini traffic:

400 \"Please use a valid role: user, model\" — the Gemini-native payload
now has a single funnel, NormalizeGeminiRequest, that hoists
system/developer-role contents into the top-level systemInstruction,
canonicalizes assistant→model, sends functionResponse-bearing turns as
user, and only lets user/model roles reach Google. TranslateOpenAIToGemini
and WrapForAntigravity both run through it, so a converter regression or
a hand-built Gemini body can no longer draw the 400. The antigravity
signature backfill also defaults every unsigned sibling call now instead
of only the first.

HTTP/2 502 on heavy prompts — the transport upgraded with
ForceAttemptHTTP2 alone leaves the h2 stack's ReadIdleTimeout at 0: a
connection that silently died (NAT drop, half-open socket) is never
probed and the request hangs until an outer layer reports an
unhelpful 502. Transports are now upgraded through x/net/http2 with
ReadIdleTimeout=2m / PingTimeout=30s, so silent-but-alive connections
are PINGed (a long prompt thinking before its first SSE byte survives)
and truly dead ones fail fast into the retry chain. The upgrade is
idempotent — Configure runs twice over the same transport in production
and a second registration panics otherwise.

go.mod/go.sum: golang.org/x/net v0.58.0 becomes a direct dependency.
